So, this idea originated because I saw a lot of people flying so slowly on RT (abt 280kts)
I realised that they wanted to fly more realistically, but in the end arent flying more realistically.
Here's why, Geo-FS uses TAS (true airspeed); which essentially adds up all of the effects of altitude to determine the true
speed of an aircraft.
In real-life, planes usually show on the primary flight display IAS (indicated airspeed); which doesn't add up the effects of 
altitude.

I thought if an autopilot was made that could suit real-life flying, it would help people actually finish an 8hr flight in 8hrs 
and not 18hrs 😭.
This is still in alpha state, so expect some bugs. 
The End.
